Setup. Let (X,d) be a metric space without isolated points. A non-autonomous dynamical system (NADS) on X is a pair (X,f_{1,∞}) where f_{1,∞}=(f_1,f_2,f_3,…) is a sequence of continuous self-maps f_i:X→X. For n≥1 set F_n = f_n ∘ f_{n-1} ∘ ⋯ ∘ f_1, and F_0 = id_X. The orbit of x∈X is orb(x,f_{1,∞}) = {F_n(x) : n≥0}.

Definitions.
• (X,f_{1,∞}) is topologically transitive if for every pair of nonempty open sets U,V⊂X there exists n≥1 with F_n(U)∩V ≠ ∅.
• A point x∈X is periodic for f_{1,∞} if there exists p≥1 with F_{kp}(x)=x for all k≥0; let Per(f_{1,∞}) denote the set of periodic points. We say "every point of X is periodic" if Per(f_{1,∞}) = X.
• A periodic point x is invariant if f_i(x)=x for some structure giving f_n(x) periodic in n; concretely, two invariant periodic points x,y are required to have disjoint orbits: orb(x,f_{1,∞}) ∩ orb(y,f_{1,∞}) = ∅.
• (X,f_{1,∞}) is finitely generated if the set {f_i : i≥1} of maps appearing in the sequence is finite; otherwise it is not finitely generated.
• (X,f_{1,∞}) is sensitive if there exists ε>0 such that for every x∈X and every neighborhood U of x there exist y∈U and n≥0 with d(F_n(x),F_n(y)) > ε.

Question. Does there exist a non-autonomous dynamical system (X,f_{1,∞}) on a metric space X without isolated points satisfying all of the following?
(1) f_{1,∞} is topologically transitive;
(2) Per(f_{1,∞}) = X;
(3) there exist two invariant periodic points x,y∈X with orb(x,f_{1,∞}) ∩ orb(y,f_{1,∞}) = ∅;
(4) (X,f_{1,∞}) is not finitely generated;
(5) (X,f_{1,∞}) is not sensitive.

